<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghazi Chelebi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1322</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a> Chelebi was the last ruler of the Pervaneid principality of Sinop on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, a descendant of the Seljuk minister Mu'in al-Din <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muin-al-din-suleyman-pervane">Pervane</a>. He was famed for naval raids against the Genoese of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feodosia">Caffa</a> and the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a>. After his death Sinop passed to the Candarids.</p></div>
